      "text": "**Config audit & fallback‑chain patch – high‑level playbook**\n\n1. **Locate the config**  \n   *Typical places:* `config/`, `etc/`, root `*.yaml|*.json|*.toml`.  \n   Run a quick inventory:  \n\n   ```bash\n   find . -type f \\( -name \"*.yaml\" -o -name \"*.yml\" -o -name \"*.json\" -o -name \"*.toml\" \\) -print\n   ```\n\n   Identify the file that defines the fallback chain (often a key like `fallback`, `fallbacks`, or `fallback_chain`).\n\n2. **Read‑only sanity check**  \n   ```bash\n   # Show with syntax highlighting (requires jq or yq)\n   cat path/to/config.yaml | yq .\n   # or for JSON\n   cat path/to/config.json | jq .\n   ```  \n\n   **What to verify:**  \n   - Presence of the `fallback_chain` (or equivalent) array/object.  \n   - No duplicate entries.  \n   - Correct ordering – higher priority first.  \n   - All referenced services/modules actually exist in the codebase (`grep -R \"<service_name>\" .`).\n\n   If the config is version‑controlled, confirm you’re on the latest stable branch:\n\n   ```bash\n   git fetch --all\n   git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD   # current branch\n   git status                         # ensure clean working tree\n   ```\n\n3. **Patch the fallback chain (read‑only → write)**  \n   Assuming you need to insert or reorder an entry:\n\n   ```bash\n   # Make a short‑lived branch\n   git checkout -b fix/fallback-chain\n   ```\n\n   **Edit the file** (use your preferred editor; `sed` can be scripted for simple inserts):\n\n   ```bash\n   # Example: prepend \"svc‑critical\" to the chain (YAML syntax)\n   yq eval '.fallback_chain = [\"svc-critical\"] + .fallback_chain' -i path/to/config.yaml\n   ```\n\n   Or for JSON:\n\n   ```bash\n   jq '.fallback_chain = [\"svc-critical\"] + .fallback_chain' path/to/config.json > tmp && mv tmp path/to/config.json\n   ```\n\n   **Validate syntax** after edit:\n\n   ```bash\n   yq test path/to/config.yaml   # yaml\n   jq . path/to/config.json > /dev/null && echo \"JSON OK\"\n   ```\n\n4. **Commit & verify**  \n\n   ```bash\n   git add path/to/config.yaml   # or .json\n   git commit -m \"Patch fallback chain: prioritize svc‑critical\"\n   ```\n\n   Run any project‑specific config lint or CI test that validates fallback logic:\n\n   ```bash\n   ./scripts/lint-config.sh   # placeholder – replace with actual command\n   ./ci/run-tests.sh          # ensure nothing else breaks\n   ```\n\n5. **Merge / PR**  \n   Push and open a PR for review:\n\n   ```bash\n   git push -u origin fix/fallback-chain\n   # then create PR via your VCS UI (GitHub, GitLab, etc.)\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### What I need from you to proceed\n1. **Exact config file path** (relative to repo root).  \n2. **Current fallback‑chain format** (YAML/JSON snippet is enough).  \n3. **Desired change** – e.g., add, remove, reorder, or replace entries, and the target ordering.  \n4. Any **project‑specific validation steps** (lint scripts, CI jobs) you expect me to run.\n\nGive me those details and I’ll supply the precise edit commands and verification checklist.",
